  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5296",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the targeting of RL95-2 through a mechanism involving Racotumomab, a drug that acts on G-protein coupled receptor 132. This relationship is supported by three distinct pathways, all of which assign doxorubicin as a target to Racotumomab, which in turn targets RL95-2. The high final scores across these paths suggest a consistent and plausible biological link between doxorubicin and RL95-2, mediated by Racotumomab. The shared involvement of Racotumomab in multiple pathways indicates a potential common mechanism, possibly involving receptor activation or downstream signaling pathways. The evidence supports a mechanistic connection where doxorubicin indirectly influences RL95-2 via Racotumomab, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of G-protein coupled receptors in mediating the effects of doxorubicin on RL95-2.",
